          "id": 4,
          "links": [],
          "title": "Headline",
          "vizConfig": {
            "group": "text",
            "kind": "VizConfig",
            "spec": {
              "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {},
                "overrides": []
              },
              "options": {
                "code": {
                  "language": "plaintext",
                  "showLineNumbers": false,
                  "showMiniMap": false
                },
                "content": "## UFOs love fireworks: July 4th is the top day of the year\n\nA typical day of the year has about 190 reports (the median is 193). July 4th has 1,208, more than six times as many, and 84 % of them come between 8 pm and midnight, when the fireworks go up.\n\nThe other spikes fall on the 1st and the 15th of a month, such as June 1st (1,140): many reports seem to carry a rounded date. Brush the day-of-year chart to see any of them on the map.\n\n**Also in the data:** most sightings happen at night, peaking in the 9 pm hour (11,445 reports); Saturday is the busiest day of the week; and reports grew from a few hundred a year before 1990 to over 7,000 a year in 2012 and 2013.\n\n*Figures counted in the dataset with SQL.*",
                "mode": "markdown"
              }
            },
            "version": "13.3.0"
          }
        }
      },
