                "content": "**The data.** The reports to the [National UFO Reporting Center](https://nuforc.org) (NUFORC), geocoded and with their times standardized by [planetsig](https://github.com/planetsig/ufo-reports) in 2014: 80,331 reports from 1906 to May 2014, mostly from the United States. A report is what someone said they saw, where and when they said it, not a verified event. The places are geocoded from the town named, the times are local as reported, and some dates were rounded by the people reporting them (the spikes on the 1st and the 15th of a month).\n\n**How it was made.** Grafana Assistant built this dashboard from one prompt for #30DayMapChallenge 2026, day 10 (Prompting only): the dataset's SQL, the Chaski filters, the Kepler Plus map and the Mosaic charts. A review then checked its figures with SQL and fixed three things: the time range (it opened on the last 30 days, which emptied the charts), the day of year (counted on a fixed calendar, so July 4th is always day 186) and the headline's figures. The CSV is converted once to Parquet by `datasets/ufo-sightings/build.sh` in [pacha-dashboards](https://github.com/ubica-ecuador/pacha-dashboards); the dataset reads it on the server and cleans it.",
                "mode": "markdown"
              }
            },
            "version": "13.3.0"
          }
        }
      }
    },
